      "turn": 1,
      "user": "Is hempcrete basically marijuana in my walls?",
      "assistant": "No, hempcrete is not marijuana in your walls! \n\nWhile both hemp and marijuana come from the *Cannabis sativa* plant family, hemp used for building materials is a completely different variety. Industrial hemp is bred to have very tall, woody stalks with extremely low levels of THC (the compound that causes a high)—typically less than 0.3%—making it entirely non-psychoactive and legally distinct from drug-type cannabis. When mixed with lime and water to create hemp-lime insulation, the plant hurds (the woody inner core) form a durable, breathable biocomposite that cannot be used for any recreational purpose.\n\nWould you like to explore how hemp-lime walls regulate moisture and indoor climate for a specific project you have in mind?",
